[tint] Use a function variable for the LoopRange loop index

Backport of https://github.com/google/dawn/pull/87 (Gerrit change 348435),
not yet in the Dawn commit Skia pins in its DEPS (third_party/externals/dawn).

Builder::LoopRange held the loop index in a block parameter of the loop body,
which the SPIR-V writer emits as an OpPhi. On a Pixel 8 (Mali-G715, driver
r54p3, Android 17) with the Vulkan backend, shaders that execute such a loop
hang the GPU and the device is lost a few seconds later. LoopRange is used on
the SPIR-V path by ZeroInitWorkgroupMemory, PreservePadding, Std140,
DecomposeAccess (whole array loads, which is how Skia Graphite's gradient
shaders read their color stops) and ForkExplicitLayoutTypes.

Hold the index in a function variable declared in the loop initializer
instead. This is the shape a WGSL `for` loop lowers to, which that driver
executes correctly.

Drop this patch once the pinned Dawn carries the change: build-dawn.ts skips
it when it is already present and fails when it no longer applies.

---
--- a/src/tint/lang/core/ir/builder.h
+++ b/src/tint/lang/core/ir/builder.h
@@ -2076,15 +2076,21 @@ class Builder {
         auto* end_value = Value(std::forward<END>(end));
         auto* step_value = Value(std::forward<STEP>(step));
 
+        // The loop index is held in a function variable rather than in a block parameter of the
+        // loop body. A block parameter becomes an OpPhi in SPIR-V, and loops with that shape hang
+        // the GPU on some Mali drivers (see https://crbug.com/568850691).
         auto* loop = Loop();
-        auto* idx = BlockParam("idx", start_value->Type());
-        loop->Body()->SetParams({idx});
+        ir::Var* idx_var = nullptr;
         Append(loop->Initializer(), [&] {
             // Start the loop with `idx = start`.
-            NextIteration(loop, start_value);
+            idx_var = Var("idx", ir.Types().ptr(core::AddressSpace::kFunction, start_value->Type(),
+                                                core::Access::kReadWrite));
+            idx_var->SetInitializer(start_value);
+            NextIteration(loop);
         });
         Append(loop->Body(), [&] {
             // Loop until `idx == end`.
+            auto* idx = Load(idx_var)->Result();
             auto* breakif = If(GreaterThanEqual(idx, end_value));
             Append(breakif->True(), [&] {  //
                 ExitLoop(loop);
@@ -2096,8 +2102,9 @@ class Builder {
         });
         Append(loop->Continuing(), [&] {
             // Update the index with `idx += step` and go to the next iteration.
-            auto* new_idx = Add(idx, step_value);
-            NextIteration(loop, new_idx);
+            auto* idx = Load(idx_var)->Result();
+            Store(idx_var, Add(idx, step_value));
+            NextIteration(loop);
         });
     }
 
